      "id": "source-3",
      "type": "review-note",
      "reviewer": "OpenAI Codex",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-24T18:58:30Z",
      "note": "Reviewed the successful exploit receipt and trace, iETH proxy creation trace, LoanTokenLogicWeth deployment, target_ storage history, exploit-time bytecode, source reproduction, and campaign-loss reporting. The exploit calls iETH proxy 0xb983e01458529665007ff7e0cddecdb74b967eb6, which delegates to 0xde744d544a9d768e96c21b5f087fc54b776e9b25. Factory 0x8cc1cfdc1c60c19a1d7c0fa3c042a4916aa79a51 created the proxy in block 10785086. The custom target_ slot 0x14 changed from 0xe8279915fe5fb202041c3b3bf97d0f95949d503f to the exploited implementation in setTarget transaction 0x689cc627a562f892ab36edd8b29c6557bedb17c78f80bb26ddaa577aa460cd6c at 2020-09-04T19:53:15Z and remained unchanged through the incident. The implementation was deployed in block 10796762 and its 20,511-byte runtime hash is 0x153147d85fddfac599aed6d58a1488595e6b12f736ad4aca8e72e1a1929ed35c at selection and exploit time. LoanTokenLogic's _internalTransferFrom cached both balances before either write and permitted sender == receiver, duplicating iTokens. The reported gross campaign loss was approximately $8.1 million: 219,199.66 LINK, 4,502.70 ETH, 1,756,351.27 USDT, 1,412,048.48 USDC, and 667,988.62 DAI; later recovery does not reduce exploit-time gross loss."
    },
